   "he": "קַנְקַנְתּוֹם — חַרְתָּא דְאוּשְׁכָּפֵי. דִּיפְתְּרָא — דִּמְלִיחַ וּקְמִיחַ וְלָא עֲפִיץ. נְיָיר — מְחָקָא.",
   "en": "«Kankantom» is what is called in Aramaic «ḥarta de’ushkafei,» a black dye used by shoemakers. «Diftera» is hide «that was processed with salt and flour, but not with gallnuts. Neyar» is known in Aramaic as «maḥaka,» paper made from reeds."
  }
